  "report_week": "30",
  "report_period": "Week 30 (17th Jul to 24th Jul 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Adani Shipping have committed their Capesize \"Aashna\" 179/2012 HHIC, Philippines (SS/DD 10/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 37,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Cape Sandra\" 175/2011 HHIC, Philippines (SS/DD 05/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold back in March at xs USD 32 mill. The Kamsarmaxes \"Nord Antares\" & \"Nord Andromeda\" 82/2022 Yamic, China (SS/DD 01/2027 & SS/DD 01/2027, Scrubber fitted) were committed to undisclosed interests at USD 37,5 mill each. Note that the one-year- younger \"Rostrum Stoic\" 82/2023 Jiangsu, China (SS 11/2028, DD 11/2026) was sold earlier this month at USD 37 mill. Santoku Senpaku have committed their Panamax \"Yarra\" 78/2015 Sasebo, Japan (SS 05/2030, DD 05/2028) to Chinese interests at mid USD 28 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Barwon\" 78/2015 Sasebo, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 01/2028) was sold back in March at xs USD 26 mill. On the Ultramax sector, Oldendorff Carriers committed their \"Benjamin Oldendorff\" & \"Britta Oldendorff\" 62/2020 Oshima, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 06/2028 & SS 04/2030, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted) to clients of Meghna at low USD 37 mill each. By way of comparison, the \"WF Artemis\" 63/2020 Iwagi, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 36,5 mill. Moreover, Wisdom Marine Lines have committed their \"Amis Wisdom VI\" 61/2011 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) at rgn USD 22 mill. Remind you that back in April, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"ASL Ixora\" 61/2012 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold at xs USD 20 mill. Yano Kaiun have committed the Supramaxes \"United Halo\" & \"Venus Halo\" 55/2012 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027 & SS/DD 02/2027) at rgn USD 19 mill each, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Lagonda\" 55/2011 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 07/2026) was sold earlier this month at USD 18,1 mill basis SS/DD passed. Furthermore, Graham Shipping committed their \"Capt Eugene\" 55/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS 06/2030, DD 09/2028) at USD 16,8 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Bermondi\" 55/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 07/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold three weeks ago at USD 15,3 mill. On the Handysize sector, Pacific Carriers committed their \"Ikan Landuk\" 37/2013 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 07/2027, OHBS) to undisclosed interests at USD 16,9 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the two-years-younger \"Shinsung Accord\" 37/2015 Saiki, Japan (SS 02/2030, DD 12/2027, OHBS) was sold at USD 19 mill. In addition, SEAMEC committed their \"Seamec Gallant\" 32/2011 Jiangmen, China (SS/DD 10/2026) at USD 9,5 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the one-year-older \"Despina K\" 32/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 05/2030, DD 09/2028) was sold at USD 9,2 mill.",
    "tankers": "",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia/China route were under pressure, with Dampier to Qingdao fixtures settling between USD 11.05/11.10 fio. In the Atlantic, departures from Tubarao and Acu to Qingdao, including West Africa options, secured between USD 32.00/34.30 fio. Further East, runs from Gladstone and HPCT to East Coast India settled at USD 20.40 fio and USD 17.40 fio respectively.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac rounds with Singapore/Japan redelivery fixed at USD 14,000 pd, while trips via Australia to China and Singapore/Japan range settled between USD 15,000/19,500 pd. Indonesian coal runs from South East Asia and South China to South China, India and local ranges fetched USD 13,000/18,000 pd. Out of India and South East Asia, trips via ECSA with Singapore/Japan and South East Asia redelivery achieved USD 17,500/22,750 pd. On period, activity was firm with vessels fixing between USD 16,000/20,500 pd for 10 to 13 months, a short 2/3 laden legs option securing USD 21,000 pd, and a 12-month deal settling at USD 18,750 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips from North China with Singapore/Japan redelivery fixed at USD 18,000 pd. From South China and South East Asia, local, clinker, and coal runs to China, South East Asia and East Coast India fetched between USD 14,500/25,000 pd, while multi-laden legs to Singapore/Japan range reached up to USD 24,000 pd. Departures from India and PG ranges for local and China trips settled between USD 15,000/21,500 pd, while a trip from West Coast India to Continent made USD 14,000 pd. In the Atlantic, a US Gulf run to Continent achieved USD 23,000 pd. Out of South Africa, coal trips to East Africa and West Coast India ranges obtained between USD 17,250/28,500 pd. On period, Ultramaxes fixed for 4/6 months duration between USD 22,500/22,750 pd, while another achieved USD 18,350 pd for 12/14 months.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "It was a quiet week for the Handymax/Handysize segment with limited reported activity. From the Black Sea and East Med, trips to Continent and Med ranges settled between USD 15,000/16,800 pd. In the Atlantic, an ECSA grain run to Singapore/Japan range achieved USD 21,500 pd. From East Africa, a prompt trip to South East Asia fixed at USD 14,000 pd."
    }
  },
